  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member who uses MPStorage, I want the app to find my storage MP and read its JSON document, so that my bookmarks, synced blacklist and MP flags follow me across clients.\n\n### Scope\n\nTwo pure parsers in HFRParsing, no network:\n1. **Find**: on an MP list page, the row of the storage thread (subject `MP_NAME`, with or without the `[non lu] ` prefix) and its `post` id; when absent, enough pager information for the caller to try the next page.\n2. **Read**: on the storage thread page, the first message's `numreponse` and the JSON text of its first `<p>` (U+00A0 removed), handed unchanged to `MPStorageCodec` (LOT-062). The \"not for you\" (`destiné`) page that legacy uses to drop a cached post id is a typed result.\n\nThe page walk, create and update writes are LOT-052. ★ Critical path: LOT-052 waits for this lot.\n\n- Module: HFRParsing · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · ★ critical path\n- Audit source: D8\n- Legacy sources (read-only; francoisgn/hfrnow at `2440d79`, an ancestor of `origin/master`):\n  - `Classes/MPStorage.m:23` (`MP_NAME`), `:692-736` (`findStorageMPFromPage:`: title of `sujetCase3` equal to `MP_NAME` or `[non lu] MP_NAME`, `post=` read from the link, page count = last child of `fondForum1PagesHaut` `div.left`, recursion to the next page) (at `2440d79`).\n  - `Classes/MPStorage.m:769-777` (thread GET URL), `:835-903` (`parseMPStorage:`: `destiné` check `:837`; second `td` of `.messagetable`, `para<numreponse>` id `:880-881`; first `<p>` text, U+00A0 removed `:882-883`; `NSJSONSerialization` `:886`; malformed JSON disables the feature `:888-891`) (at `2440d79`).\n  - Oracle analysis: LOT-004 spec, rows `mpstorage-page` and `mpstorage-op` `find`, quirks 16 and 18-20, results RC4.6 and RC4.7.\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-038-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-023 (#51, done)\n- LOT-030 (#57, done)\n- Reads, never changes: the LOT-013 (#46, done) and LOT-062 (#87, done) document types and codec.\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged, and the captures exist: `R60a`/`R60b` and their oracles were merged in #259.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- `R60a` (storage thread, first post) and `R60b` (its edit form) in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures/`, with LOT-004 oracles `Fixtures/LOT-004/R60a.oracle.json` and `R60b.oracle.json` (#259). Both hold the empty legacy document only.\n- `R13u1`, `R13u1b` (storage thread on page 1) and `R13a` (no storage thread), with the `find` oracles `Fixtures/LOT-004/S-find-*.oracle.json`.\n- *Pending capture*: a document with other clients' namespaces, member pseudos, near the 64 KiB cap or with a non-BMP character (#272, waits for an operator decision); an MP list page past the last page (#114); the `destiné` page and a storage thread found on page 2 or later (no capture issue yet). List them in the spec, never hand-build them (LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Pending captures\n\n- CAP-mpstorage-thread-its-first-post-page (#132): closed, captured as `R60a`/`R60b` (#259).\n- #272: MPStorage document with other clients' data, pseudos, near 64 KiB or non-BMP (open).\n- #114: MP list page past the last page (open).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Differential test: `find` on `R13u1`, `R13u1b` and `R13a` gives the same result as the `S-find-*` oracles (post id on page 1; none on `R13a`).\n- [ ] Differential test: on `R60a`, `numreponse` equals the oracle's `sNumRep`, and the JSON text decoded by `MPStorageCodec` equals the oracle's `dData`; the text reaches the codec byte for byte (no `Double` rewrite of numbers).\n- [ ] Title match is exact on `MP_NAME` and `[non lu] MP_NAME` only; a title that merely contains it does not match.\n- [ ] Pager information comes from the LOT-022 pager, not legacy's \"last child of `div.left`\" (windowed pager, LOT-004 RC4.6): intentional difference stated in the spec.\n- [ ] Malformed JSON, a missing first message and the `destiné` page are typed errors or results, never an empty document (legacy disabled the feature, quirk 18); states not captured are *pending capture* in the spec.\n- [ ] `JSONValue`, `MPStorageCodec` and the LOT-013 types unchanged (core-model guard, EXTERNAL-AGENTS §3).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-038-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n### Old issue (frozen)\n\n[francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#71](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/71) — read-only history.\n",
